## 8. Backend API

Extend the existing backend rather than creating conflicting endpoints.

If the project already uses `/api/v1`, preserve that version prefix.

Implement or adapt the following endpoints:

### Product endpoints

- `GET /api/v1/products` — list active products with pagination, search, and filters.
- `GET /api/v1/products/:id` — retrieve a product.
- `POST /api/v1/products` — create a product; admin only.
- `PATCH /api/v1/products/:id` — update product details; admin only.
- `DELETE /api/v1/products/:id` — archive a product by default; admin only.
- `GET /api/v1/admin/products` — list all products, including inactive ones.
- `POST /api/v1/admin/products/import` — import the initial catalog securely, with duplicate detection and a dry-run option.
- `POST /api/v1/admin/uploads/signature` — generate a short-lived Cloudinary upload signature if signed uploads are used.

### Category endpoints

- `GET /api/v1/categories`
- `POST /api/v1/categories` — admin only.
- `PATCH /api/v1/categories/:id` — admin only.
- `DELETE /api/v1/categories/:id` — admin only, with product-reference checks.

### Order endpoints

- `GET /api/v1/admin/orders` — paginated order list.
- `GET /api/v1/admin/orders/:id` — full order details.
- `PATCH /api/v1/admin/orders/:id/status` — update order status.
- `PATCH /api/v1/admin/orders/:id` — update permitted order fields.
- `POST /api/v1/orders` — create a customer order.
- `GET /api/v1/orders/track/:trackingToken` — expose only the minimum information necessary for order tracking, with appropriate access controls.

Use the existing route conventions if they differ. Validate inputs and return consistent JSON responses.

